Adding to the toolbar is slot-addressed, not index-addressed. `customControls` is a `Partial<Record<ControlSlot, CustomToolbarControl | CustomToolbarControlList>>`, so each of `first`, `second` and `third` takes either a single control object or an array of them.

A `CustomToolbarControl` is `{ component, position? }`, where `component` matches `ToolbarControlComponent` — a function taking `{ document?: PHDocument }` and returning `JSX.Element | null`. The toolbar passes the document it is operating on, which is the `document` prop when given and the currently selected document otherwise, so a custom control must treat `document` as optional.

```tsx
<DocumentToolbar
  document={document}
  customControls={{
    second: {
      position: "end",
      component: ({ document }) => (
        <button onClick={() => alert(document?.header.name)}>custom two</button>
      ),
    },
  }}
/>
```

Two behaviours worth internalising:

- **`position` defaults to `"start"`.** A custom control renders *before* the slot's built-in controls unless you set `position: "end"`. This surprises people who expect appended controls.
- **Lists need a `key`.** When a slot receives a `CustomToolbarControlList`, each item is a `CustomToolbarControl & { key: React.Key }`. The key is passed straight to React; there is no implicit index fallback.

The mutual exclusivity with `children` is enforced by the type system, not by a runtime warning. `DocumentToolbarProps` is a union of `DocumentToolbarWithChildrenProps` (document, toolbarContainer, toolbarClassName, children) and `DocumentToolbarWithCustomControlsProps` (those three plus enabled/disabled controls, componentOverrides, customControls, controlsContainer, controlsContainerClassName). In `children` mode the toolbar renders only the children inside the toolbar container, so `customControls` and every other customization prop is unused — the slots themselves stop existing.

_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/06-DocumentTools/00-DocumentToolbar.mdx, confirmed against packages/design-system/src/connect/components/document-toolbar/types.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._
